The Contractor shall provide medical travel services in response to a worldwide medical event for NASA’s Human
Spaceflight Mission Directorate (HSMD), Johnson Space Center (JSC), or other travelers identified by NASA
(referred to as ‘traveler(s)’ throughout) on a pre-paid basis regardless of traveler’s home location or country of
origin. These services include the following:
a. Provide transportation of patient from site of injury to appropriate medical facilities;
b. Coordinate with medical providers to ensure timely access to medical care;
c. Provide pharmacy assistance;
d. Obtain medical monitoring;
e. Provide assistance obtaining medications, vaccines, blood transfers, and medical devices;
f. Obtain medical referrals and consultations with English-speaking doctors;
g. Provide patient advocacy;
h. Provide bed side case management services such as in-person interaction and care;
i. Provide medical translation and interpretation services to include telephonic language assistance with medical
incidents and medical translations of medical records to the extent required to resolve the medical emergency;
j. Coordinate uninterrupted hospital admittance and discharge;
k. Coordinate hospital payments including direct billing between insurer, medical provider and traveler, without
any involvement or responsibility of the Government;
l. Coordinate insurance information between the patient, insurers, and medical providers, without any
involvement or responsibility of the Government;
m. Provide Guarantee of Payment (GOP) services and pay medical costs as an agent for the traveler to ensure
timely care and immediate discharge. The Contractor and the traveler will handle all subsequent GOP and pay
as agent reimbursements directly between themselves. The Government has no involvement, liability, or
responsibility for these financial transactions;
n. Provide repatriation of mortal remains for travelers to the location specified by NASA;
